# Exam-Buddy — Trae AI Project Rules & Guidelines

This file configures Trae AI to follow the exact same architecture, tech stack conventions, and team protocols as Antigravity and Cursor.

---

## 1. Project Tech Stack
- **Framework:** Next.js 16 (App Router)
- **Directory Root:** All frontend code resides inside `frontend/`
- **Language:** TypeScript 5+ (Strict Mode)
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS v4 (Obsidian glassmorphic dark theme, CSS variables in `globals.css`)
- **Icons:** Lucide React (`lucide-react`)
- **Backend / Database:** Supabase (PostgreSQL, pgvector, Auth, Storage)

---

## 2. Directory Architecture
- Pages & Routes: `frontend/src/app/`
- Reusable UI Components: `frontend/src/components/` (e.g. `frontend/src/components/subjects/`, `frontend/src/components/layout/`)
- Helper Utilities & Mock Data: `frontend/src/lib/`
- TypeScript Types: `frontend/src/types/`
- Custom React Hooks: `frontend/src/hooks/`

---

## 3. Team Collaboration & Git Protocol
- **NEVER** push or commit directly to `main`.
- Always work in dedicated feature branches: `feature/<member>-<feature-name>`.
- Always run `npm run build` inside `frontend/` to verify TypeScript compile safety before committing.
- Clean conventional commit format (e.g., `feat: implement flashcards spaced repetition engine`).
- Never overwrite or delete teammate components without checking first.

---

## 4. Design & Aesthetics Standard
- Obsidian dark glassmorphism: `#0B0F17` / `#131926` background, subtle glow borders (`border-white/[0.08]`), vibrant accents (indigo, violet, emerald, amber).
- Never render raw unstyled HTML elements; use polished Tailwind and Lucide components.
- Ensure full mobile and desktop responsiveness.
